# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Deep End, Same Beat

**Story & Context:** At 132 BPM, Darius opens with a rigid two-bar Club Anchor built from clustered kicks, one hard clap, rimshot, and clipped vocal syllable. Ana strikes the same waterphone rod four times while moving from LEVEL to LEFT tilt. Each attack begins similarly, but every decay bends differently as the water shifts. Mina holds one baritone-sax F through the section as Sax Buoy. Theo plays a short minor-7 Wurlitzer shell every four bars and never follows the waterphone pitch. In the refrain, a Reservoir Drop removes kick and sub during the strongest low metallic swell, then the unchanged club beat returns immediately.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Empty swimming-pool deep end with a painted depth number, one waterphone reflected in a shallow maintenance puddle, hard fluorescent light, blue tile and rusted steel. Original sparse lyric fragments: “deep end / same beat / water moved first / I stayed on the mark.”

## Track 2: The Level Line Bent After Midnight

**Story & Context:** At 136 BPM, this is the EP’s fastest and driest track. Keshawn’s vocal chops become part of the percussion, while Theo reduces Wurlitzer to two-note sus2 stabs. Ana performs repeated two-rod cells while rotating the instrument slowly clockwise. Pitch Spill becomes the hook: each second strike changes direction during decay. Darius keeps the Club Anchor unchanged for thirty-two bars. Mina answers only the final perceived pitch of every fourth spill. Midway through, a Dry Shock Bar removes the waterphone completely, making the beat sound unnervingly straight before a rapid rotating tilt state creates a Liquid False Drop without any added drum layer.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Pool-wall level line under fluorescent light, warped by a thin sheet of water running down tile, handwritten midnight maintenance note taped beside it, baritone-sax bell reflected in stainless steel. Original sparse lyric fragments: “level line / bent after midnight / don’t move the beat / let the water lie.”

## Track 3: Reservoir Empty, Rod Still Ringing

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 128 BPM and begins without sub-bass. Theo plays widely spaced 6/9 Wurlitzer chords while Ana bows one waterphone rod briefly, then stops and lets the unstable decay continue. Mina holds a low saxophone fifth for eight bars at a time. Darius uses the sparsest kick pattern on the EP and leaves entire half-bars empty. In the final minute, Keshawn stops the frame drum, Theo mutes Wurlitzer, and Mina ends her final reference tone. Ana performs one last strike while slowly tilting FORWARD. Darius keeps the Club Anchor for two cycles after the acoustic pitch has almost disappeared, then cuts the entire beat. The EP ends on the final natural metal resonance with no effect tail added.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Drained reservoir chamber after shutdown, one waterphone on a concrete floor beneath a painted fill line, fluorescent lamps switching off in sequence, one metal rod still vibrating. Original sparse lyric fragments: “reservoir empty / rod still ringing / nothing left to rise / keep the beat until it’s gone.”

